{
  "introspected": "2026-09-10",
  "why": [
    "The GRDB mirror is generated from THIS file, and this file is written from a live",
    "introspection of Supabase (information_schema + pg_catalog) — never from",
    "the web app's generated Supabase types, which declared 17 tables while the app queried 29 and",
    "has fourteen call sites silently typed `any`.",
    "",
    "Column syntax is `name:pgtype`, with a trailing `?` meaning NULLABLE IN POSTGRES.",
    "Nothing is defaulted to zero on the way in: `nil` is not `0` in at least three",
    "places in this app that have caused real bugs, and the mirror is not the layer",
    "that gets to erase the distinction.",
    "",
    "FOUR live tables are deliberately absent:",
    "  · body_measurements — the tape TABLE. It stays out: a table of girths is a",
    "    screen of girths, and that has been removed from the product twice.",
    "    REVISED 2026-09-17 (W3): the ONE measurement the athlete actually takes",
    "    is now a column, `daily_logs.waist_cm`, beside the weight it belongs",
    "    with. A column on the day is not a tape table — there is one number, it",
    "    sits in the reading it was taken with, and there is still nowhere for",
    "    hips, thighs or arms to land.",
    "  · notion_credentials, notion_exports — the Notion integration was deleted on",
    "    2026-08-22 and these two are waiting on drop-SQL.",
    "  · widget_tokens — dies with the token-authenticated snapshot endpoint the",
    "    moment the App Group exists.",
    "That leaves the 29 the app actually reads.",
    "",
    "`bespoke: true` means the table is NOT generated. Three of them already exist",
    "locally in a DIFFERENT shape that the logger owns — `workout_sets.set_index` is",
    "`set_number` here, `workout_sessions.date` does not exist here at all — so they",
    "are pulled through SyncTranslation into the tables that are already there,",
    "rather than mirrored beside them under a second name.",
    "",
    "`since: 2` marks a table added by W2 (2026-09-10). The generator emits those into",
    "`migrateMirrorV2` so a store that already ran v9 creates them at v21 and a fresh",
    "install creates both sets in order. Columns W2 added to OLDER tables are listed in",
    "`cols` (so a fresh install gets them at v9) AND altered in by `v21.genericModel`",
    "for stores that already exist -- the same guarded shape `v13.supplementArchive` uses.",
    "",
    "The W2 columns on OLDER tables are nullable HERE even where Postgres declares them",
    "NOT NULL DEFAULT: the DDL is pasted by hand, and a pull of `plans` that ran before",
    "the paste must not fail to decode a row the server has always served. nil reads as",
    "the default (`is_legacy` false, `sort` 0, `kind` day) and `encodeIfPresent` keeps the",
    "column out of a push body until Postgres grows it -- the `sleep_inaccurate` rule.",
    "",
    "`since: 3` marks the table added by the export v6 wave (2026-09-20): `prescriptions`,",
    "the CURRENT instruction per movement, appended and never overwritten. The generator",
    "emits it into `migrateMirrorV3`, which `v33.prescriptions` registers; a fresh install",
    "runs V1, V2 and V3 in order. `daily_logs.hrv_overnight` is a column on an OLDER table",
    "and follows the v21 rule -- listed in `cols` for a fresh install and altered in by the",
    "same migration for a store that already exists. It was introspected live on 2026-09-20",
    "and had been missing from this file since it was written.",
    "",
    "`custom_supplements.dose_periods` (App Store sprint W5, 2026-09-23) is the same shape of",
    "change: a column on an OLDER table, listed in `cols` for a fresh install and altered in by",
    "`v35.dosePeriods` for a store that already exists. It was ABSENT when this line was written",
    "-- `docs/sql/w5-dose-periods.sql` is the founder's paste -- and it is nullable in Postgres",
    "too, so a nil keeps it out of every push body until a dose actually changes.",
    "",
    "`custom_supplements.other_ingredients` (overhaul Lane C, 2026-09-24) is the same shape",
    "again: a jsonb string array of the label ingredients the nutrient table has no key for,",
    "written only by the DSLD import and altered in by `v38.otherIngredients`. The Postgres",
    "half is in the Lane C wave record and is pasted by hand BEFORE the first import -- a row",
    "that carries the key is refused by PostgREST until the column exists."
  ],
  "strategies": {
    "cursor": "Delta by a monotonic timestamp column. Only trustworthy on a table whose updated_at is maintained by the server-side trigger; a client-written timestamp from a slow phone lands in the past and is skipped forever.",
    "window": "A trailing window on a date/timestamp column, for the append-mostly day-keyed tables that carry no updated_at. Misses an edit to a row older than the window; realtime is what catches those.",
    "full": "Small and rarely written. Cheaper to re-read than to reason about."
  },
